# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The virtio console driver PD, both ways. It refuses and counts the
# client's malformed record; the client's two lines go out through the
# console, QEMU loops them back (virtio-console-test.qemu), and they reach
# the client, control characters printed as dots.
NOWAYOS: virtio-console: starting
NOWAYOS: virtio-console: ready: transmit and receive, on transport 7
NOWAYOS: serial-test: starting
NOWAYOS: virtio-console: refused so far: 1 malformed chunk(s) from the client, 0 malformed queue entries from the device, 0 corrupt ring(s)
NOWAYOS: serial-test: sent two lines
NOWAYOS: serial-test: received: a line from the guest, out through the console and back
NOWAYOS: serial-test: received: control characters: . a bell, . a tab

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# or the driver or client giving up.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
